# INERT: reviewed destination is .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/submit-tip.yml.
name: Submit an accepted tip
description: Opt in one agent-assisted merged pull request for curator review.
title: '[Tip] '
body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        Submit as the GitHub account that authored the pull request. One issue covers one PR.
        This public issue is a request for curator review, not automatic enrollment.
        The board counts one point per eligible merge, not value or verified AI use.
        Only eligible public repositories and non-bot authors can count. Self-owned or controlled projects do not qualify.
        Do not post secrets, private repository details, or personal data beyond the public identities needed for this submission.
  - type: input
    id: pull_request
    attributes:
      label: Public merged pull request
      description: Canonical https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/number URL.
      placeholder: https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/number
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: checkboxes
    id: declarations
    attributes:
      label: My declarations for this pull request
      options:
        - label: I am the pull request author, submitting through that same GitHub account.
          required: true
        - label: I used agent assistance for this pull request. This is my declaration, not independently verified AI use.
          required: true
        - label: I do not own or control the receiving repository, organization, or project.
          required: true
        - label: I explicitly opt in this pull request and my public GitHub identity, submission proof, merge facts, and nullable change-size context for the Tipjar public board.
          required: true
        - label: I understand that a curator must accept this submission, and that editing this issue pauses counting until reviewed again.
          required: true
        - label: I understand that withdrawing or an accepted owner opt-out removes current rows on a successful refresh; failures can delay removal until displayed expiry. Public issues, source history, old artifacts, and caches may retain earlier data.
          required: true
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        To withdraw, edit this issue to say "I withdraw my opt-in" and notify curators here.
        Closing the issue alone does not withdraw. Editing changes the reviewed body digest,
        suppressing this consent on the next refresh; another separately reviewed consent issue can still qualify the same PR.
        Curators remove all consent entries for a withdrawn tip and recompute current totals.
        Repository owners/maintainers can request an opt-out through a public issue; curators verify their role independently.
        Enrollment never grants source approval, local execution permission, or publication authority for new work.
